---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "@lucide/astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Speaking"
  description="Invite Makayla Ferrell to speak at your event — cybersecurity topics made clear and accessible for every audience."
  active="speaking"
>
  <section
    aria-labelledby="speaking-heading"
    class="overflow-hidden px-5 pt-16 pb-20 sm:px-8 md:pt-24"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
      <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
        <!-- Text column -->
        <div class="max-w-xl">
          <!-- Badge -->
          <div
            class="border-line bg-surface text-muted mb-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs shadow-sm"
          >
            <span class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#28C840]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            SPEAKING
          </div>

          <!-- Headline -->
          <h1
            id="speaking-heading"
            class="text-brand mb-6 font-serif text-4xl leading-[1.15] sm:text-5xl md:text-[3rem]"
          >
            Cybersecurity that makes sense to every audience.
          </h1>

          <!-- Body -->
          <p class="text-muted mb-8 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed">
            Makayla Ferrell is a former software developer turned penetration tester, educator, and
            founder of QueryLock. She makes complex cybersecurity and technology topics clear,
            useful, and relevant for audiences ranging from developers and security teams to
            students, business leaders, and people with no technical background.
          </p>

          <!-- CTAs -->
          <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-3">
            <a
              href="/contact"
              class="focus-ring bg-accent hover:bg-accent-deep inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full px-7 py-3 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-colors"
            >
              Invite Makayla to Speak <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="#experience"
              class="focus-ring border-accent text-accent hover:bg-tint inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-7 py-3 font-sans text-sm font-semibold transition-colors"
            >
              View Speaking Experience
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Image placeholder column -->
        <div class="flex justify-center lg:justify-end">
          <div
            class="border-line bg-surface flex w-full max-w-sm flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 rounded-2xl border-2 border-dashed py-24 lg:max-w-none"
            aria-label="Placeholder for professional photo of Makayla speaking"
          >
            <Image size={32} class="text-line" aria-hidden="true" />
            <p class="text-muted font-sans text-xs">professional photo of Makayla speaking</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- ─── Perspective section ─── -->
  <section
    id="experience"
    aria-labelledby="perspective-heading"
    class="bg-band px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
      <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
        <!-- Text column -->
        <div class="max-w-xl">
          <h2
            id="perspective-heading"
            class="text-brand mb-6 font-serif text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl md:text-[2.5rem]"
          >
            A perspective from both sides of software security.
          </h2>
          <div class="text-muted space-y-5 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Before testing applications for vulnerabilities, Makayla built software herself. That
              experience gives her a practical understanding of how developers think, the pressures
              engineering teams work under, and why security guidance can succeed or fail in the
              real world.
            </p>
            <p>
              Her work in penetration testing showed her the other side: how attackers find
              weaknesses, how small decisions become security risks, and how often the same problems
              appear because the people building and using technology were never given the context
              to understand them.
            </p>
            <p>
              Whether the room is full of developers, security professionals, students, executives,
              or people who have never written a line of code, Makayla meets the audience where they
              are and makes the technology understandable without talking down to them.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Journey visual column -->
        <div class="flex justify-center lg:justify-end">
          <div class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-2xl bg-white px-10 py-14 lg:max-w-none">
            <ol
              class="flex list-none flex-col items-center gap-0 p-0"
              aria-label="Makayla's career journey"
            >
              {
                ["DEVELOPER", "PENETRATION TESTER", "EDUCATOR", "FOUNDER"].map((label, i, arr) => (
                  <>
                    <li class="bg-band text-accent w-full rounded-full py-2.5 text-center font-sans text-xs font-bold">
                      {label}
                    </li>
                    {i < arr.length - 1 && (
                      <li
                        aria-hidden="true"
                        class="text-muted py-2 text-base leading-none select-none"
                      >
                        ↓
                      </li>
                    )}
                  </>
                ))
              }
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
